  "notes": [
    "Periods: Early 1806-1808, Middle 1809-1812, Late 1813-1814.",
    "Detached Elite Companies: a brigade's battalions may lose their Light and/or Grenadier companies to form combined Tiny/Small/Standard-sized detachment units, addable to any Infantry Brigade — see p.101 of the book for the full conversion table.",
    "Household Cavalry (1st/2nd Life Guards, Royal Horse Guards) saw little Peninsular action; include 1 to 3 at the listed cost if desired.",
    "Half battery: pay half points (rounded up) to field an artillery battery at half strength.",
    "This builder omits the book's many point-modifier upgrades/downgrades (Large, Small, Veteran status, Ferocious Charge swaps, etc.) — apply these manually per the book when finalising a list.",
    "Allies: not specified beyond the Portuguese integration above.",
    "Named commanders have no official points cost in this supplement — priced here at the generic Divisional Commander cost for their Staff Rating; adjust freely."
  ]
}
